  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$ of equal masses are suspended from two massless springs of spring constant $\\mathrm{k}_1$ and $\\mathrm{k}_2$, respectively. If the maximum velocities, during oscillation, are equal, the ratio of amplitude of $A$ and $B$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_1}{\\mathrm{k}_2}}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{k}_1}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{k}_1}}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_1}{\\mathrm{k}_2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{V}_{\\max }=\\omega \\mathrm{A}=\\mathrm{m} \\omega^2 \\mathrm{I}=\\mathrm{k}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\omega^2=\\frac{\\mathrm{k}}{\\mathrm{m}} \\Rightarrow \\omega=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}}{\\mathrm{m}}} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\omega \\propto \\sqrt{\\mathrm{K}} \\quad$ or $\\quad \\frac{\\omega_1}{\\omega_2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_1}{\\mathrm{k}_2}}$\n$\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{A}} \\max =\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{B}} \\max \\quad \\Rightarrow\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_1}{\\mathrm{~m}}}\\right)\\left(\\mathrm{A}_1\\right)=\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{~m}}}\\right)\\left(\\mathrm{A}_2\\right) \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{A}_1}{\\mathrm{~A}_2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{k}_1}}$"
  }
}